r \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: You know, while we have the time --\par \par \uc2 DANA JACOBSON: I did, but by accident. It was closer to that --\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: While we have the time here. I think we can talk at the table a little bit about my glasses.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Okay.\par \par \uc2 DANA JACOBSON: We like the glasses.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: So Katy picked them out. Father Time made them necessary, and I will say that times have changed since I was in middle school. Shanta Fripp, our director, said you know, it looks great.\par \par \uc2 DANA JACOBSON: We love them.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: You guys supported them. There`s no "Kick me" sign on my back.\par \par \uc2 DANA JACOBSON: They look good.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: They look great.\par \par \uc2 DANA JACOBSON: And you can see.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: I can see. That`s the most important thing.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Clark Dokoupil. That`s for sure.\par \par \uc2 All right, Jericka talks with Patti LaBelle. You don`t want to miss this.\par \par \uc2 (ANNOUNCEMENTS)\par \par \uc2 (LOCAL NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (LOCAL WEATHER)\par \par \uc2 (ANNOUNCEMENTS)\par \par \uc2 **********************************(08:00AM, EDT)**********************************\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Welcome back to CBS MORNINGS. I`m Tony Dokoupil.\par \par \uc2 Coming up in this hour, the legendary Patti LaBelle for today`s "Morning`s Mixtape." She tells Jericka Duncan why she is not done climbing.\par \par \uc2 DANA JACOBSON: I`m Dana Jacobson. Oliver Jeffers creates visual worlds that kids love to dive into. He`ll have perspective on his latest book about a family road trip through space.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: I`m Nate Burleson. If you can go anywhere in the world right now, where would it be? We`ll look at the new "Conde Nast" Traveler poll filled with great recommendations from your fellow adventurer.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: All right, you`ll take the kids, right?\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: No.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: But first, here`s today`s "Eye Opener at Eight."\par \par \uc2 Russia unleashes more missile strikes as Ukraine gains ground, and President Biden warns that Putin is not joking about using nukes.\par \par \uc2 CHARLIE D`AGATA: According to a British Intelligence report today, Ukrainians have captured so many Russian tanks at least 440.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Sources tell CBS News, the \uc2 FBI\uc2  believes it has enough evidence for criminal charges against \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 CATHERINE HERRIDGE: The lawyer for the President`s son slammed the allegations as inaccurate and claimed \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  is a target simply because of his family name.\par \par \uc2 DANA JACOBSON: President Biden says he`ll pardon all federal offenses for simple possession of marijuana.\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 : I`m calling on all Governors to do the same for State marijuana possession offenses. Too many lives have been upended because of our failed approach to marijuana.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Gas prices in California surge $1.15 in a single month.\par \par \uc2 PATRICK DE HAAN: We`ve never seen the gap between California and the rest of the country this high.\par \par \uc2 MAN: He said he wanted to serve in the military again.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: And in a touching ceremony, a World War Two vet is sworn in as an honorary member of the Michigan National Guard for his 100th birthday.\par \par \uc2 MAN: He served his nation not once, but twice.\par \par \uc2 (GROUP singing "Happy Birthday.")\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: That`s awesome.\par \par \uc2 DANA JACOBSON: Looking pretty good for a hundred.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Yes.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: You know, when you serve, you leave, but you still serve, right? And they brought him back. You never really go.\par \par \uc2 DANA JACOBSON: It stays with you.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Beautiful.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: That was awesome.\par \par \uc2 DANA JACOBSON: It stays with you.\par \par \uc2 We`re going to start this hour with our series "Morning`s Mixtape" showcasing the brilliant career of the great, Patti LaBelle. The Godmother of Soul is known for her incredible voice and is no stranger to TV viewers either.\par \par \uc2 (Clip from "A Black Lady Sketch Show.")\par \par \uc2 DANA JACOBSON: Whether she is singing, acting, or cooking up one of her famous meals, LaBelle has been an entertainment fixture for more than half a century.\par \par \uc2 Our national correspondent, Jericka Duncan caught up with her during a rare moment of downtime.\par \par \uc2 Jericka, good morning.\par \par \uc2 JERICKA DUNCAN: Good morning. You can tell I had fun with this exciting story.\par \par \uc2 Even the pandemic couldn`t slow down Miss Patti LaBelle. She has continued to show up for her fans. She did a streaming battle with Gladys Knight. She sang at the Macy`s Thanksgiving Day Parade and the National Tree Lighting Ceremony, and she recently appeared on the popular podcast, "Drink Champs" with N.O.R.E. and DJ EFN.\par \par \uc2 But the living legend tells us, there is nothing like performing in front of a live audience.\par \par \uc2 (Begin VT)\par \par \uc2 PATTI LABELLE: A lot of people when they meet me they say. "Are you still working? Are you still touring?" I say, "\uc2 Google\uc2  me, Boo."\par \par \uc2 Because I am always on the run. I`m booked and busy and blessed.\par \par \uc2 JERICKA DUNCAN: Not bad and bougie. Booked, booked, and blessed.\par \par \uc2 PATTI LABELLE: That`s it.\par \par \uc2 JERICKA DUNCAN: Okay.\par \par \uc2 It`s a life 78-year-old, Patti LaBelle has never taken for granted.\par \par \uc2 (Clip from Patti LaBelle performance.)\par \par \uc2 JERICKA DUNCAN: She is touring 11 months this year, captivating crowds as she has done for over 60 years.\par \par \uc2 PATTI LABELLE: Usually on stage, I have my shoes on the piano, and then I -- if I kick off a shoe, I`ll go right to the piano and put another one on.\par \par \uc2 (Clip from Patti LaBelle performance.)\par \par \uc2 JERICKA DUNCAN: At a recent concert, her signature siren brought down the house, even as the skies opened up.\par \par \uc2 Her steps to start began at church.\par \par \uc2 PATTI LABELLE: My mother made me go to choir rehearsal night because she heard my voice, and I was very shy I said, "Well, I don`t want to go." And the Choir Director said, "You should be a lead singer."\par \par \uc2 JERICKA DUNCAN: Did you have stage fright at that point?\par \par \uc2 PATTI LABELLE: Yes. I`m still shy. Very shy.\par \par \uc2 JERICKA DUNCAN: So what happens when you get out on the stage?\par \par \uc2 PATTI LABELLE: Everything. A whole another Patti comes out.\par \par \uc2 (Clip from Patti LaBelle and the Blue Belles performance.)\par \par \uc2 JERICKA DUNCAN: That other Patti became the lead vocalist for Patti LaBelle and the Blue Belles, which rose to national acclaim performing at the Apollo Theater.\par \par \uc2 Then a major reset. The group, Labelle was formed, which included Nona Hendryx and Sarah Dash.\par \par \uc2 (Clip from Labelle performance.)\par \par \uc2 JERICKA DUNCAN: By 1975, a major hit was born.\par \par \uc2 PATTI LABELLE: I knew it was a hit never knowing what it meant.\par \par \uc2 (Clip from Labelle performance.)\par \par \uc2 PATTI LABELLE: Patti singing a song, and I was clueless about hookers. So, it was a hit, a hooker hit.\par \par \uc2 JERICKA DUNCAN: Labelle became the first African-American group to play at New York`s Metropolitan Opera House, and the first to land the cover of "\uc2 Rolling Stone\uc2 " Magazine.\par \par \uc2 In 1983, Patti went out on her own as a solo artist.\par \par \uc2 (Clip from "On My Own.")\par \par \uc2 JERICKA DUNCAN: She has won two Grammys, several Lifetime Achievement Awards, and she has also earned the title, Godmother of Rock and Soul.\par \par \uc2 Do you embrace that title?\par \par \uc2 PATTI LABELLE: Heck, yes. I love it.\par \par \uc2 JERICKA DUNCAN: What does it mean to you when you hear that?\par \par \uc2 PATTI LABELLE: It means that I`m good. It means that I`m listened to. It means that I`m embraced by a lot of people and I love it.\par \par \uc2 (Clip from "Live: One Night Only.")\par \par \uc2 JERICKA DUNCAN: A Godmother to many, a friend and mentor to artists like Mariah Carey, Jazmine Sullivan, and Ledisi, who all plan to join her on a new R&B album.\par \par \uc2 PATTI LABELLE: Twenty songs, some collaborations, a lot of surprises.\par \par \uc2 JERICKA DUNCAN: You did jazz. You did gospel. You`ve constantly been reinventing yourself. Is that intentional?\par \par \uc2 PATTI LABELLE: Yes. Very intentional. You don`t want to become boring to people.\par \par \uc2 (Clip from "In the Neighborhood.")\par \par \uc2 JERICKA DUNCAN: LaBelle is anything but boring. When she is not singing or acting.\par \par \uc2 (Clip from "In the Neighborhood.")\par \par \uc2 JERICKA DUNCAN: She is cooking up ideas as an entrepreneur. Remember those famous Patti LaBelle sweet potato pies?\par \par \uc2 (Clip from James Wright.)\par \par \uc2 JERICKA DUNCAN: She is now expanding her brand, Patti`s Good Life.\par \par \uc2 PATTI LABELLE: And dip --\par \par \uc2 JERICKA DUNCAN: With her grandchildren in mind.\par \par \uc2 PATTI LABELLE: I have pancakes and waffles and the inspiration are those two little girls, you know, so that I can make good breakfast for them.\par \par \uc2 (Clip from Patti LaBelle performance.)\par \par \uc2 JERICKA DUNCAN: It is the family she has left that feeds her soul.\par \par \uc2 She lost her mother to diabetes, and three sisters to cancer.\par \par \uc2 How did that shape how you see the world?\par \par \uc2 PATTI LABELLE: It just helped me see the world as tomorrow is not promised.\par \par \uc2 (Clip from Patti LaBelle performance.)\par \par \uc2 JERICKA DUNCAN: She recalled one of her biggest regrets, not making her sister, Jackie, a sandwich the day before she died.\par \par \uc2 PATTI LABELLE: You just feel like sometimes you don`t want to be bothered, which is human, but then when something like that happens, you put things in perspective and you say, "Okay, for the rest of my life I`m not going to ever deny no matter how tired I am."\par \par \uc2 JERICKA DUNCAN: So Patti LaBelle gives with her talents, her time, and her attention, especially to the fans.\par \par \uc2 WOMAN: Her voice is so strong and her music has so much meaning.\par \par \uc2 WOMAN: It transcends.\par \par \uc2 WOMAN: She is just so soulful.\par \par \uc2 JERICKA DUNCAN: Even in this downpour --\par \par \uc2 WOMAN: I could listen to her all day and all night.\par \par \uc2 (Clip from Patti LaBelle performance.)\par \par \uc2 JERICKA DUNCAN: The crowd was swept away by that memorable voice that`s reigned for decades.\par \par \uc2 (Clip from Patti LaBelle performance.)\par \par \uc2 JERICKA DUNCAN: I`ve heard you say, "Oh, I`m not really a big star yet."\par \par \uc2 PATTI LABELLE: I am not. As far as me being that real super, super, super superstar woman, I`m not there yet.\par \par \uc2 (Clip from Patti LaBelle performance.)\par \par \uc2 PATTI LABELLE: Ami pleasant with who I am and happy? I`m ecstatic. I love the Patti LaBelle that`s here now. And she`s going to climb higher, but this one is good. She`s real good.\par \par \uc2 (Clip from Patti LaBelle performance.)\par \par \uc2 (End VT)\par \par \uc2 JERICKA DUNCAN: Patti LaBelle. She was incredible.\par \par \uc2 DANA JACOBSON: Oh my goodness.\par \par \uc2 JERICKA DUNCAN: That was like a moment -- when I got the call asking, like, hey, are you available to do this piece? I`m like, absolutely.\par \par \uc2 DANA JACOBSON: I`ll make myself available.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Of course.\par \par \uc2 JERICKA DUNCAN: Yes. So I have to give you guys some background.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Okay.\par \par \uc2 JERICKA DUNCAN: You see how giving she is with her time.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Yes.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Yes.\par \par \uc2 JERICKA DUNCAN: And you know when we go out on these shoots, you have a certain amount of time.\par \par \uc2 DANA JACOBSON: Yes.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: And it is business.\par \par \uc2 JERICKA DUNCAN: It is business. Right? In and out. But we stayed and we played cards with Miss Patti. Pitty Pat is one of her favorite card games. She even lent me some money, so I could stay to play the card game. I had to win back the money because I said, "I will be you know what if I leave this house," and I owed Patti LaBelle some money.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: What?\par \par \uc2 JERICKA DUNCAN: How did that look like?\par \par \uc2 DANA JACOBSON: That`s awesome.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Wow.\par \par \uc2 JERICKA DUNCAN: But we had a lot of fun. She was showing me some of the shoes that she puts on that piano and kicks off, so I think we have some video of me trying on her lovely shoes. Look at those.\par \par \uc2 DANA JACOBSON: At 78.\par \par \uc2 JERICKA DUNCAN: Right there. Look at those shoes, at 78 and she will wear a heel, but that one right there.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Look at you trying them all.\par \par \uc2 JERICKA DUNCAN: I am secretly praying, like maybe she is going to give me these Louis Vuitton.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: As a parting gift. Did she give you a pair shoes?\par \par \uc2 JERICKA DUNCAN: No. No shoes. But you know what? She gave us plenty to remember. Great memories, and I was invited back to do a little bit of cooking.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: I`m coming.\par \par \uc2 JERICKA DUNCAN: Yes.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: It sounds like you lose at cards, so she`s happy about that.\par \par \uc2 DANA JACOBSON: Yes, she will bring you down.\par \par \uc2 JERICKA DUNCAN: Yes, and this really comes full circle. I was telling my mother who met Patti LaBelle backstage about 20 plus+ years ago. There she is right there 