s the sign of a good airline and I think places like \uc2 JetBlue\uc2  --\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Yes.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Erin Florio, you`re the best. Appreciate you.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 ERIN FLORIO: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: We`ll be right back.\par \par \uc2 (ANNOUNCEMENTS)\par \par \uc2 DANA JACOBSON: Coming up: Best-selling children`s author, Oliver Jeffers talks about the big ideas in his newest picture book and the unexpected path that led him to kiddy lit stardom.\par \par \uc2 You`re local news is next.\par \par \uc2 (LOCAL NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (LOCAL WEATHER)\par \par \uc2 (ANNOUNCEMENTS)\par \par \uc2 *************************************************************************** ** (08:30 AM, EDT)\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Welcome back to CBS MORNINGS. It is time to bring you some of the stories that are the talk of the table this morning, and Tony you are kicking us off.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Oh, okay. Since I got my glasses on and someone on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  said, I look like an English Lit professor. I have got a little history lesson on marijuana decriminalization.\par \par \uc2 DANA JACOBSON: Okay.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Okay.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: It`s about the last Democratic President to push forward in any way at all, and in fact, this was somebody who went way further than President Biden. I`m talking about Jimmy Carter in the summer of 1977, who wrote a seven-page letter to Congress in which he called for the abolishment of all criminal penalties for the simple possession of marijuana.\par \par \uc2 And in the famous quote, what he said is, "Penalties against possession of a drug should not be more damaging to an individual than use of the drug itself." That was 1977.\par \par \uc2 And then I went and took a look at how the election turned out for Jimmy Carter, he lost 47 states.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Forty seven?\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Now, that`s 