ion even if you`re using it.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: It`s amazing.\par \par \uc2 JAMIE YUCCAS: That`s interesting. I knew mine was on never, but now I want to look and see if I did the precise location.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Precisely.\par \par \uc2 DAVID BEGNAUD: I looked at mine, it was on, so I turned it off.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: I didn`t know there was that lower one I`ve got it on never.\par \par \uc2 You know, if \uc2 Instagram\uc2  had like a team of guys with clipboards following you down the street, you`d be really weirded out.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Yes.\par \par \uc2 JAMIE YUCCAS: And that`s pretty much what they`re doing.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: That`s pretty much what they`re doing.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: And the reality is, some people don`t care.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Honestly, most people.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Almost prefer it.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Yes, most people that I`ve talked to and I`ve covered this for years, they just don`t care as long as they`re getting a better user experience.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Exactly.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: That`s the bottom line.\par \par \uc2 DAVID BEGNAUD: Okay. I turned it off.\par \par \uc2 Listen, we`ve got to follow up on Vanessa Bryant, Kobe Bryant`s widow and that $16 million award from her lawsuit over the graphic photos of her husband and daughter`s bodies.\par \par \uc2 Vanessa Bryant will reportedly donate the payout to the nonprofit of Mamba and Mambacita Sports Foundation. Kobe Bryant created that foundation back in 2016 to offer sports education to underserved athletes.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, you might remember a jury found that the LA County Sheriff`s Office and the Fire Department were liable for distress caused by photos that first responders took and then shared after the chopper crash that killed Kobe and Gianna Bryant and seven others back in 2020.\par \par \uc2 JAMIE YUCCAS: You know, she, at the beginning of this t