)\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: The band is multi-platinum selling and has earned a reputation as one of the greatest live acts on the planet. They sell out arenas and stadiums all around the world and their ninth studio album "Will of the People" is out today. What a coincidence.\par \par \uc2 Anthony Mason joins us from California where he spoke with Muse, frontman, Matt Bellamy.\par \par \uc2 Anthony, I hope you went to a live concert. Good morning.\par \par \uc2 ANTHONY MASON: Good morning.\par \par \uc2 Funny how that happens.\par \par \uc2 Matt Bellamy says Muse has always dabbled with the dark side and when the pandemic hit, he felt the band had no choice, but to delve into dystopian doom and gloom once again.\par \par \uc2 (Begin VT)\par \par \uc2 (Clip from Muse performance.)\par \par \uc2 ANTHONY MASON: "Will of the People," the new album by the British band, Muse was written in Matt Bellamy`s Santa Monica studio.\par \par \uc2 MATT BELLAMY (Muse frontman): We are going into the red room, which is --\par \par \uc2 ANTHONY MASON: The red room?\par \par \uc2 MATT BELLAMY: Yes. Which -- are you a "Twin Peaks" fan?\par \par \uc2 ANTHONY MASON: I am a "Twin Peaks" fan.\par \par \uc2 MATT BELLAMY: Yes, so maybe you`ll recognize this space. So, in "Twin Peaks," whenever they have the weird nightmares.\par \par \uc2 ANTHONY MASON: Yes.\par \par \uc2 MATT BELLAMY: And it goes into the strange where everyone`s speaking backwards.\par \par \uc2 (Clip from "Twin Peaks.")\par \par \uc2 MATT BELLAMY: This is the space, so I wanted to model it exactly like the "Twin Peaks" red room. So, here we go.\par \par \uc2 ANTHONY MASON: That`s an interesting inspiration.\par \par \uc2 (Clip from Muse performance.)\par \par \uc2 ANTHONY MASON: Bellamy is the band`s lead singer and songwriter.\par \par \uc2 MATT BELLAMY: I`ve got all of my favorite toys here. This synth here was the first synth I ever had. I was about 12 years old; I think.\par \par \uc2 ANTHONY MASON: And you still 